3>\n        <a href=\"/matchbox-cars/matchbox-cars-entry-13\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Matchbox entry 13\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Supporting entry under Matchbox.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Contains\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/matchbox-cars/matchbox-cars-entry-14\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Matchbox entry 14\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Supporting entry under Matchbox.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Figures are the primary trailheads for this subject graph.</li><li>Matchbox sources is a primary trailhead under Matchbox.</li><li>Matchbox geography is a primary trailhead under Matchbox.</li><li>Matchbox legacy is a primary trailhead under Matchbox.</li><li>Evidence around Matchbox is classified as documented on Ton-o-Lore.</li><li>Matchbox currently maps to 39 linked entities inside Matchbox.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"sources\">\n    <h2>Sources &amp; further reading</h2>\n    <p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matchbox\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Fandom wiki</a></p>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is Matchbox?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        Matchbox belongs to Matchbox. A matchbox is a container or case for matches, made of cardboard, thin wood, or metal, generally in the form of a box with a separate drawer sliding inside the cover.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Matchboxes generally measure 5 x 3.5 x 1.5 cm, and commonly have coarse striking surfaces on the edges for lighting the matches. Cylindrical matchboxes with a round cover on one end are also available.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        There are metal matchboxes some of which also have a hollow cylinder in which a nitrated wick is housed so that it can ignite when it is windy. The metal boxes have a scraper that is usually placed on the edge, in a slot made for this purpose.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        A sort of file that can be machined to the same metal casing or be a metal sheet, welded or glued.\n    </p>\n    \n</section>","word_count":816,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"a8a6e559-7204-4c8d-9688-c4ddc5fc8622","name":"Matchbox","slug":"matchbox-cars","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"Matchbox belongs to Matchbox. A matchbox is a container or case for matches, made of cardboard, thin wood, or metal, generally in the form of a box with a separate drawer sliding inside the cover.","description":"Matchbox belongs to Matchbox. A matchbox is a container or case for matches, made of cardboard, thin wood, or metal, generally in the form of a box with a separate drawer sliding inside the cover.\n\nMatchboxes generally measure 5 x 3.5 x 1.5 cm, and commonly have coarse striking surfaces on the edges for lighting the matches. Cylindrical matchboxes with a round cover on one end are also available.\n\nThere are metal matchboxes some of which also have a hollow cylinder in which a nitrated wick is housed so that it can ignite when it is windy. The metal boxes have a scraper that is usually placed on the edge, in a slot made for this purpose.\n\nA sort of file that can be machined to the same metal casing or be a metal sheet, welded or glued.","evidence":"documented","universe":"matchbox-cars","aliases":["Matchbox"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[{"id":"6a8e6846-6461-4463-b8b8-ba7c493eda00","relationship":"contains","title":"Figures are the prim